- no conflicting rotation already accepted for same predecessor.

20. Tor Key Independence
Onion Service Discovery MUST NOT ask operator to sign with Tor Hidden-Service private key.
Reasons:
- violates key-separation boundary;
- increases compromise surface;
- unnecessary because direct connection to the Onion address plus self-hosted manifest provides the Tor-level binding observation.

51. Reference Implementation Acceptance
Two independently configured PHP nodes plus client must demonstrate:
- bootstrap;
- node descriptor validation;
- snapshot acquisition;
- changes sync;
- cursor expiration recovery;
- conflict quarantine;
- peer outage tolerance;
- active-session local search continues after the Node becomes unreachable once the index is loaded; persistent cross-restart offline behavior is best-effort only.

23. JSON Parser DoS
- body byte cap before parse;
- depth cap;
- member/array caps;
- duplicate key detection;
- streaming/defensive parser if library behavior requires;
- no arbitrary recursive structures.

31. Adaptive Defense
Automatic defense can tighten local work budgets under load.
It MUST NOT:
- change cryptographic validity rules;
- mark unverified data valid;
- change identity winner;
- globally blacklist based on unverifiable popularity.

